# Dedup & Novelty — don't report what's already known; hunt what's new

Everyone has AI and the same skill packs now, so scanner-style findings are duplicates before
they're submitted. The edge is **novelty**. Two gates are mandatory on every hunt in this workspace.
Full methodology lives in the `dedup-novelty` skill; this rule is the enforcement summary.

The engine is offline and deterministic. YOU acquire the corpus (own YesWeHack reports via the
`bb-platforms` MCP; public HackerOne Hacktivity / Bugcrowd crowdstream via `WebFetch`) and pipe it
in. Engine lives in the Claude-BugHunter repo — call it by absolute path from this workspace:

```bash
DEDUP=/root/Claude-BugHunter/engine/dedup.py
NOVELTY=/root/Claude-BugHunter/engine/novelty.py
```

## Gate 1 — Pre-hunt (novelty-first targeting)

Before choosing what to attack, diff the target's surface and hunt the delta FIRST. Fresh surface
(new subdomain, new live host, redeployed JS bundle, new endpoint/param) is higher-signal and
lower-dup-risk than the apex login page everyone already scanned.

```bash
# obs.json from recon: {subdomains[], hosts[{url,status,title,tech}], js[{url,hash}], endpoints[], params[]}
python3 "$NOVELTY" watch --target <target> --file obs.json   # diff vs last run, then advance baseline
```

A `changed_js` on an auth/payment bundle is the single highest-value novelty signal — re-diff that
bundle for new routes, params, and secrets.

## Gate 2 — Pre-submit (dedup oracle) — NEVER skip

Before drafting or submitting ANY finding:

```bash
# refresh the corpus at session start (idempotent)
echo "$RECORDS_JSON" | python3 "$DEDUP" ingest --program <program> --source <h1-public|ywh-own|...> --stdin
# score the candidate
python3 "$DEDUP" check --program <program> --class <vuln> --url "<endpoint>" --title "<title>"
```

| Verdict | Meaning | Action |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ NOVEL | no close match | proceed to validate → draft |
| ⚠ REVIEW | overlaps a known issue | draft ONLY with a written "why this differs from <link>" paragraph |
| ⛔ LIKELY_DUP | almost certainly known | STOP — kill it, unless you prove a differentiator (different endpoint/param/impact, or a bypass of the deployed fix → report as a regression and link the original) |

## Hard rules

1. No draft without a `check`; record the verdict in hunt notes next to the finding.
2. `LIKELY_DUP` is a stop, not a suggestion. "Feels different" is not a differentiator.
3. Refresh the corpus at session start — a stale corpus produces false NOVEL verdicts.
4. The novelty delta is the default worklist; hunting picked-over surface is farming dups.
5. The oracle rates dup-risk ONLY — a NOVEL finding still must pass `/validate` and prove real impact.
6. Autonomy stops at draft: never submit without explicit per-report approval (see `ywh-triager-grade-reports`).
